{#- The footer, once, instead of seven times. It was already identical on all
    seven pages apart from four stray blank lines on the home page, so it takes
    no parameters at all.

    This is where the duplication was worst: her phone number was written out 55
    times across the site and her email 18. Both now come from _data/site.json,
    which is also what the admin panel will write to. -#}
<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="footer-grid">
      <div class="footer-col footer-brand">
        <a class="brand" href="index.html">
          <svg class="brand__mark" viewBox="0 0 64 34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M3 24h6M55 24h6M9 24c0-3 2.4-5.4 5.4-5.4S19.8 21 19.8 24 17.4 29.4 14.4 29.4 9 27 9 24Z"/>
            <path d="M44 24c0-3 2.4-5.4 5.4-5.4S54.8 21 54.8 24s-2.4 5.4-5.4 5.4S44 27 44 24Z"/>
            <path d="M19.8 24h24.4"/>
            <path d="M4 21c1-5.5 3-8 6-8.6l9-5.2c2-1.2 4.3-1.6 6.6-1.2l14 2.6c2 .4 3.8 1.4 5.2 2.9l4.4 4.6 8 1.8c3 .7 4.8 2.5 4.8 5"/>
            <path d="M17 12.4h13.6M33 8.2 36 15"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="brand__text">
            <span class="brand__name">{{ site.name }}</span>
            <span class="brand__tag">{{ site.tagline }}</span>
          </span>
        </a>
        <p>Mobile interior auto detailing across Pierce County. Owned and operated by Ava Bright.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-col">
        <h4>Pages</h4>
        <ul>
{%- for item in site.nav %}
          <li><a href="{{ item.href }}">{{ item.label | safe }}</a></li>
{%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-col">
        <h4>Service area</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><p>All of {{ site.area.county }}, {{ site.area.region }}</p></li>
{#- The towns were a second hand-written list sitting next to the one the schema
    uses. Same seven names, batched three to a line, so there is one place to
    add a town and it lands in the footer and the structured data together. -#}
{%- for row in site.area.cities | batch(3) %}
          <li><p>{{ row | join(" &middot; ") | safe }}</p></li>
{%- endfor %}
          <li><a href="contact.html">Somewhere else? Ask.</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-col">
        <h4>Get in touch</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="tel:{{ site.phone.tel }}">{{ site.phone.display }}</a></li>
          <li><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></li>
          <li><a href="contact.html">Request a quote</a></li>
          {# The Google listing is filed under "Attention to Detail Auto", the
             name on the profile rather than the name on the site. Linking it
             from every page is the one signal that ties the two together for
             anyone checking she is real. #}
          <li><a href="{{ site.google }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Find me on Google</a></li>
          <li><a href="{{ site.facebook }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Facebook</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="footer-bottom">
      <p>&copy; 2026 {{ site.name }} &middot; Interior Auto Detailing</p>
      <p class="spacer">Site by Gaspar Web Co.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
